Description: native GNOME photograph culling and selection suite
 Photo Selector Linux is a high-performance native GNOME photograph
 culling and comparison selection suite built for Debian 13 (Trixie)
 and modern Linux desktops.
 .
 Key features:
  * 1-Up, 2-Up, and 3-Up Focus Mode with tactile Sliding Triplet navigation
  * Real-time noise-corrected 2D Laplacian focus sharpness scoring (< 2.0ms)
  * Non-destructive transactional file operations with copy-undo safety
  * Native Libadwaita Studio Dark theme and zero-latency keyboard routing
  * Support for camera RAW formats, JPEG companions, and XMP sidecars
